Mixing units is the commonest error: a cutting speed in m/min with a diameter in mm, or a force in kN with an area in mm squared, without the conversion factor.

Other common errors are:
confusing tolerance with clearance, or precision with accuracy;
quoting a standard or code clause without checking the edition and the country it applies to;
treating a textbook process as universal when it depends on the material and the machine;
forgetting tooling, setup time, scrap and inspection when estimating cost;
assuming lean tools such as kanban work without stable demand and quality;
accepting software output as correct because it looks precise.

State your assumptions. An examiner, like a plant manager, needs to see how you reached the answer as well as the answer itself.
